Nexus-BS: late IAA quarantine, no doorbell over a pending one, bulk IN streams, STALL only on
a real halt, NAK reload, overlay toggle, timeout diagnostics, no sleep in the critical section.

- A cycle the watchdog ends with USBCMD.IAAD still set (late) hands its URBs back but
  quarantines its QHs (and their qTDs): not reusable until a doorbell rung later, with IAAD
  clear, has been answered by a real IAA. No doorbell is rung while IAAD is set (the late IAA
  would end the new cycle and free QHs unlinked after its doorbell); waiting QHs are deferred,
  retried by the watchdog poll, and after CONFIG_USB_EHCI_IAA_WATCHDOG_US of a stuck doorbell
  handed back quarantined. Only quarantined QHs left: an empty doorbell releases them.
- usbh_kill_urb() waits for its IAA cycle without sleeping in the OSAL critical section:
  after CONFIG_USB_EHCI_IAA_SPIN_US it releases it at every nesting level for each 1 ms sleep
  (usb_osal_crit_suspend/resume); the QH generation stops the wait if it was reused.
- USBH_EHCI_URB_STREAM: bulk IN URBs (<= 16 KiB, one qTD) of an endpoint chain on one QH
  that ends at a dummy qTD, appended as Linux qh_append_tds() (fill the dummy, link a new one,
  activate last); the toggle stays in the overlay. Retired qTDs complete their URBs while the
  QH stays linked; an empty or halted stream is unlinked and the URBs left on it come back
  after its IAA cycle (-USB_ERR_SHUTDOWN unless they finished, progress from the overlay).
  USBH_EHCI_URB_APPEND_ONLY refuses to start a new stream (-USB_ERR_BUSY).
- Errors as Linux qtd_copy_status(): transaction or data buffer errors are -USB_ERR_IO also
  when they halted the qTD; only a halt without them is -USB_ERR_STALL (stock reported a
  STALL for exhausted transaction errors and reset the toggle).
- High-speed bulk QHs get the NAK count reload EHCI_TUNE_RL_HS (4) as Linux qh_make().
- Every bulk completion takes its data toggle from the stable QH overlay at hand-back.
- Timeout diagnostics: usbh_ehci_diag_capture/print (QH, overlay, qTD chain, async ring
  membership and length, USBCMD/USBSTS/ASYNCLISTADDR, FRINDEX twice, PORTSC1, IAA state and
  counters since the last successful completion), rate limited (usbh_ehci_diag_allowed); a
  synchronous URB that times out is captured twice 100 ms apart before its cancel.

